Measured, \code{names(formals(graphics::fourfoldplot))} is exactly
\verb{x, color, conf.level, std, margin, space, main, mfrow, mfcol} -- no
\code{xlab}, no \code{ylab}, no \code{...} -- and \code{fourfoldplot(tab, xlab = "X")}
stops with "unused argument". Reading a label that the function rejects
would be dead code asserting an argument that cannot exist.
